    "summary": "High‑energy Weather Report Suite, tight China>Rider, epic Other One",
    "blurb": "The show shines with a monster Weather Report Suite and a seamless China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider transition. Jerry delivers sweet vocals and soaring leads while Phil supplies a priceless bass splurge on the Rider solo. Highlights include an expansive The Other One segue from Nobody's Fault but Mine and a rare Wharf Rat → Stella Blue pairing.",
    "review": "On December 8, 1973 at Cameron Indoor Stadium, the Dead were in top form, charging through a marathon first set that built to a soaring Weather Report Suite – Prelude, Part 1 and Let It Grow – where Jerry’s guitar soars over Phil’s funk‑filled bass. The second set never lets up: a tight China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider jams into an explosive Other One after a gritty Nobody's Fault but Mine, while Keith Godchaux adds shimmering piano textures on They Love Each Other and during the Rider solo. Rare moments like the Wharf Rat → Stella Blue segue and tender ballads such as Me And Bobby McGee give the evening both drama and intimacy. The Miller soundboard capture (gd1973-12-08.sbd.miller.105607.flac16) preserves the nuance of this high‑energy performance, making it a must‑listen for anyone exploring the 1973 era.",
